{"id":"d4ae73c2fc9ccebd","group":"67","path":"67/67-df-irredundant-axiomatization.md","title":"Irredundance and Effective Irredundant Axiomatization","display":"df-irredundant-axiomatization — Irredundance and Effective Irredundant Axiomatization","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom","book_abbrev":"67","label":"67-df-irredundant-axiomatization","aliases":["67-df-irredundant-axiomatization"],"display":"df-irredundant-axiomatization — Irredundance and Effective Irredundant Axiomatization","depends_on":["[[67-df-recursively-enumerable-theory]]","[[67-df-theory-closed]]","[[67-df-prim-provability]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li\\[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)\\[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf","source_edition":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition","source_chapter":"4","source_label":"chapter opening and §2 definitions","source_printed_pages":"52,57,70","source_pdf_pages":"63,68,81","verification_status":"source-statement-checked","source_proof_status":"定义陈述及有效性条件已核对；不涉及定理证明","eligible_as_verified_dependency":true},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"67"},{"key":"label","html":"67-df-irredundant-axiomatization"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>67-df-irredundant-axiomatization</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-irredundant-axiomatization — Irredundance and Effective Irredundant Axiomatization"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ae4400eaf5ddc9a9\" href=\"?note=ae4400eaf5ddc9a9\" title=\"67-df-recursively-enumerable-theory\">67-df-recursively-enumerable-theory</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"6062469a25ee5f89\" href=\"?note=6062469a25ee5f89\" title=\"67-df-theory-closed\">67-df-theory-closed</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"573b4c635ea6d91f\" href=\"?note=573b4c635ea6d91f\" title=\"67-df-prim-provability\">67-df-prim-provability</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition"},{"key":"source_chapter","html":"4"},{"key":"source_label","html":"chapter opening and §2 definitions"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"52,57,70"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"63,68,81"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"定义陈述及有效性条件已核对；不涉及定理证明"},{"key":"eligible_as_verified_dependency","html":"true"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span> 是有效一阶语言，固定有效 Gödel 编号 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g\">\\(g\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,U,X\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\">\\(T,U,X\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cn}_L\">\\(\\mathrm{Cn}_L\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"6062469a25ee5f89\" href=\"?note=6062469a25ee5f89\" title=\"67-df-theory-closed\">67-df-theory-closed</a>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{REAx}\">\\(\\mathrm{REAx}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"ae4400eaf5ddc9a9\" href=\"?note=ae4400eaf5ddc9a9\" title=\"67-df-recursively-enumerable-theory\">67-df-recursively-enumerable-theory</a>，有限可推导性见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"573b4c635ea6d91f\" href=\"?note=573b4c635ea6d91f\" title=\"67-df-prim-provability\">67-df-prim-provability</a>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ax}_T(X,U)\">\\(\\mathrm{Ax}_T(X,U)\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Irred}_T(X)\">\\(\\mathrm{Irred}_T(X)\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IA}_T(U)\">\\(\\mathrm{IA}_T(U)\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ExistsIrred}_T(U)\">\\(\\mathrm{ExistsIrred}_T(U)\\)</span> 在下式定义，都是元语言谓词。量词中的句子集不预设可枚举；只有显式的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{REAx}\">\\(\\mathrm{REAx}\\)</span> 要求有效性。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{Ax}_T(X,U)&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Cn}_L(T\\cup X)=\\mathrm{Cn}_L(U),\\\\\n\\mathrm{Irred}_T(X)&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\forall\\varphi\\in X\\ \\bigl(T\\cup(X\\setminus\\{\\varphi\\})\\nvdash\\varphi\\bigr),\\\\\n\\mathrm{IA}_T(U)&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\exists X\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{REAx}(X)\\land\\mathrm{Ax}_T(X,U)\\land\\mathrm{Irred}_T(X)\\bigr),\\\\\n\\mathrm{ExistsIrred}_T(U)&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\exists X\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{Ax}_T(X,U)\\land\\mathrm{Irred}_T(X)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{Ax}_T(X,U)&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Cn}_L(T\\cup X)=\\mathrm{Cn}_L(U),\\\\\n\\mathrm{Irred}_T(X)&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\forall\\varphi\\in X\\ \\bigl(T\\cup(X\\setminus\\{\\varphi\\})\\nvdash\\varphi\\bigr),\\\\\n\\mathrm{IA}_T(U)&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\exists X\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{REAx}(X)\\land\\mathrm{Ax}_T(X,U)\\land\\mathrm{Irred}_T(X)\\bigr),\\\\\n\\mathrm{ExistsIrred}_T(U)&amp;\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\exists X\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{Ax}_T(X,U)\\land\\mathrm{Irred}_T(X)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>印刷52页在第4章开头明确规定：相对公理化 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T+X\">\\(T+X\\)</span> 要求新公理集 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> 递归可枚举。57页的 i.a. 沿用该规定，而“<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> 不可冗余”这个集合性质本身没有有效性条件。因此本册用 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IA}_T\">\\(\\mathrm{IA}_T\\)</span> 对应原书 i.a.，另以 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ExistsIrred}_T\">\\(\\mathrm{ExistsIrred}_T\\)</span> 明示任意集合的版本；二者不能互换。绝对 i.a. 是 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IA}_{\\varnothing}\">\\(\\mathrm{IA}_{\\varnothing}\\)</span>。</p>\n<p>印刷70页进一步指出：Theorem 4.7 的理论有一个不可冗余的非r.e.公理集，但没有不可冗余的r.e.公理化。空新公理集也允许，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Irred}_T(\\varnothing)\">\\(\\mathrm{Irred}_T(\\varnothing)\\)</span> 按全称量词空真；本定义不把理论强制等同于其演绎闭包。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"67-df-recursively-enumerable-theory","status":"resolved","id":"ae4400eaf5ddc9a9","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-recursively-enumerable-theory]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-theory-closed","status":"resolved","id":"6062469a25ee5f89","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-theory-closed]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-prim-provability","status":"resolved","id":"573b4c635ea6d91f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-prim-provability]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-theory-closed","status":"resolved","id":"6062469a25ee5f89","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$L$ 是有效一阶语言，固定有效 Gödel 编号 $g$，$T,U,X\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L$；$\\mathrm{Cn}_L$ 见 [[67-df-theory-closed]]，$\\mathrm{REAx}$ 见 [[67-df-recursively-enumerable-theory]]，有限可推导性见 [[67-df-prim-provability]]。","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-recursively-enumerable-theory","status":"resolved","id":"ae